1
00:00:05,170 --> 00:00:06,210
Hello?

2
00:00:06,380 --> 00:00:08,380
- Hey, Joey! JOEY     - Hey, Pheebs.

3
00:00:08,590 --> 00:00:09,840
Can you do me a favor?

4
00:00:10,050 --> 00:00:13,420
I forgot the PIN to my ATM card. Can you get it for me?

5
00:00:13,630 --> 00:00:14,680
Sure. Where is it?

6
00:00:14,840 --> 00:00:17,930
Uh, I scratched it on the ATM machine on the corner.

7
00:00:18,850 --> 00:00:20,890
Oh, so you're 5-6-3-9?

8
00:00:21,100 --> 00:00:22,770
That's it! Thanks.

9
00:00:24,310 --> 00:00:26,810
- Wanna talk to Chandler?     - Let me talk to him.

10
00:00:27,020 --> 00:00:28,810
He didn't believe in my movie...

11
00:00:29,020 --> 00:00:33,240
...which is a big mistake, because it is real. Real.

12
00:00:33,950 --> 00:00:35,610
I've tried to apologize.

13
00:00:35,860 --> 00:00:39,410
If I can't do it on the phone, I'll go and do it in person.

14
00:00:39,620 --> 00:00:41,660
I heard that. Uh, can you put him on?

15
00:00:41,830 --> 00:00:42,870
Yeah.

16
00:00:44,910 --> 00:00:46,370
- Hey.     - Don't come out here.

17
00:00:48,500 --> 00:00:51,920
I support you 100 percent and I wanna prove that to you in person.

18
00:00:52,130 --> 00:00:55,380
I got that. I forgive you. Don't come out here.

19
00:00:55,590 --> 00:00:57,760
You haven't taken my calls for a week.

20
00:00:57,970 --> 00:01:01,810
I'm totally over it. Friends forever. Don't come out here.

21
00:01:03,180 --> 00:01:05,480
Would you mind doing a picture with us?

22
00:01:06,310 --> 00:01:07,350
Uh, what was that?

23
00:01:07,560 --> 00:01:09,350
Uh, Entertainment Tonight.

24
00:01:11,520 --> 00:01:14,490
Good talking to you and don't come out here.

25
00:01:54,980 --> 00:01:56,030
Monica?

26
00:01:56,280 --> 00:01:58,740
I'm sorry I'm late.

27
00:02:01,910 --> 00:02:03,200
Monica?

28
00:02:04,290 --> 00:02:05,330
Phoebe?

29
00:02:06,960 --> 00:02:09,370
I'm so sorry. Have you been here long?

30
00:02:09,580 --> 00:02:11,250
That's okay.

31
00:02:12,290 --> 00:02:14,040
What the hell took you so long?

32
00:02:16,210 --> 00:02:18,880
You can't tell Chandler. I ran into Richard.

33
00:02:19,090 --> 00:02:20,550
- Which Richard?     - The Richard.

34
00:02:20,760 --> 00:02:22,930
Richard Simmons? Oh, my God!

35
00:02:24,220 --> 00:02:28,520
No, my ex-boyfriend Richard. You know, the tall guy, mustache.

36
00:02:28,730 --> 00:02:32,100
Okay, that actually makes more sense. How was it?

37
00:02:32,310 --> 00:02:36,110
It was really nice. We talked and I had lunch with him.

38
00:02:36,320 --> 00:02:39,440
That's weird. I dreamed you had lunch with Richard.

39
00:02:39,650 --> 00:02:41,570
- Really?     - Again, Richard Simmons.

40
00:02:42,320 --> 00:02:43,370
Go on.

41
00:02:43,620 --> 00:02:46,080
The strange part was he was really nice...

42
00:02:46,290 --> 00:02:49,200
...and he looks great, but I didn't feel anything.

43
00:02:49,410 --> 00:02:51,250
So why can't we tell Chandler?

44
00:02:51,460 --> 00:02:56,040
It'll freak him out and tomorrow's our anniversary. I don't wanna spoil it.

45
00:02:56,250 --> 00:02:59,340
I can't believe you guys have lasted a whole year!

46
00:02:59,550 --> 00:03:01,840
Wow, I owe Rachel 20 bucks.

47
00:03:02,890 --> 00:03:03,930
What?

48
00:03:04,140 --> 00:03:05,930
On a totally different bet.

49
00:03:08,270 --> 00:03:09,310
Hey!

50
00:03:09,480 --> 00:03:11,940
- It's almost our anniversary!     - I know.

51
00:03:12,150 --> 00:03:15,230
One year ago today, I was just your annoying friend Chandler.

52
00:03:15,400 --> 00:03:18,900
Aw, now you're just my annoying friend Chandler.

53
00:03:19,490 --> 00:03:21,570
- Huh.     - I got you a gift.

54
00:03:21,780 --> 00:03:25,570
- It's not till tomorrow.     - I know, but you have to open it today.

55
00:03:38,250 --> 00:03:40,420
Okay! There you go!

56
00:03:40,670 --> 00:03:43,340
- It's two tickets to Vegas!     - Wow.

57
00:03:43,510 --> 00:03:46,470
Yeah! For this weekend! It'll be perfect.

58
00:03:46,680 --> 00:03:50,810
You'll see Joey, plus, we'll start our celebration on the plane.

59
00:03:51,060 --> 00:03:54,100
We can call it our "Plane-a-versary."

60
00:03:55,190 --> 00:03:56,230
We have to?

61
00:03:58,360 --> 00:04:01,650
This is great, but Joey didn't want any of us there.

62
00:04:01,860 --> 00:04:06,570
He doesn't want us to go to any trouble. He'll be excited when we surprise him.

63
00:04:06,820 --> 00:04:10,660
Plus, we get to have our own "Anna-Vegas-ry"!

64
00:04:12,710 --> 00:04:15,290
"Anna-vada-versary!"

65
00:04:16,130 --> 00:04:18,750
I think we should see other people.

66
00:04:18,960 --> 00:04:20,300
We can go, right?

67
00:04:20,590 --> 00:04:21,800
Great idea.

68
00:04:22,010 --> 00:04:23,300
I'm gonna go too!

69
00:04:26,470 --> 00:04:28,600
Pheebs, it's kind of our anniversary.

70
00:04:28,810 --> 00:04:31,560
You won't ditch me like you did with London.

71
00:04:31,770 --> 00:04:33,600
Ditch you? You were pregnant...

72
00:04:33,770 --> 00:04:35,350
Uh-huh. Great story. I'm going.

73
00:04:38,310 --> 00:04:40,190
- Hi.     - Hey.

74
00:04:40,400 --> 00:04:44,650
Listen, this weekend we're all gonna go to Las Vegas to surprise Joey!

75
00:04:46,610 --> 00:04:48,160
Including me!

76
00:04:48,830 --> 00:04:49,870
Do you wanna go?

77
00:04:50,080 --> 00:04:51,990
I can take a couple days off work.

78
00:04:52,200 --> 00:04:56,620
Of course you can take a couple days off, because this trip includes me!

79
00:04:58,460 --> 00:05:01,710
I've got a presentation tomorrow. I can't miss that.

80
00:05:01,920 --> 00:05:05,970
I've got tickets to the Van Gogh exhibit. I waited a year for this.

81
00:05:06,800 --> 00:05:10,100
- Rach, maybe we can fly out Saturday?     - Sounds great.

82
00:05:10,310 --> 00:05:11,760
I'll call the airlines.

83
00:05:12,680 --> 00:05:15,600
That'll be nice to have the apartment to myself.

84
00:05:16,270 --> 00:05:17,770
To walk around naked.

85
00:05:20,270 --> 00:05:23,730
No, so I can be by myself. Have a little alone time.

86
00:05:24,320 --> 00:05:25,610
Naked alone time.

87
00:05:26,490 --> 00:05:30,070
Just because I'm alone doesn't mean I wanna walk around naked.

88
00:05:30,330 --> 00:05:32,700
You live alone, you don't walk around naked.

89
00:05:32,910 --> 00:05:35,830
Uh-huh. Why does it takes me so long to answer the door?

90
00:05:42,460 --> 00:05:47,130
So far, is this trip to Las Vegas better or worse than the trip to London?

91
00:05:47,380 --> 00:05:50,010
So far, it's pretty much the same, Pheebs.

92
00:05:50,760 --> 00:05:53,970
What about after I give you these candies?

93
00:05:55,310 --> 00:05:57,680
- I guess it's a little better now.     - Ha, ha.

94
00:05:58,440 --> 00:06:01,900
Las Vegas, 1. London, 0.

95
00:06:02,520 --> 00:06:03,570
I'll be back.

96
00:06:07,360 --> 00:06:08,950
Happy Plane-a-versary.

97
00:06:09,490 --> 00:06:12,160
Aw. I love you.

98
00:06:12,410 --> 00:06:15,240
- Can I give you your present now?       - Okay!

99
00:06:19,870 --> 00:06:21,830
Oh, don't tell me I did this.

100
00:06:22,090 --> 00:06:25,460
I love "I forgot the present" fake-out!

101
00:06:26,170 --> 00:06:29,880
How about "I did forget the present, forgive me" not fake-out?

102
00:06:30,470 --> 00:06:32,890
You can give it to me when we get back.

103
00:06:33,140 --> 00:06:35,510
This is the worst thing that could happen.

104
00:06:35,720 --> 00:06:38,640
You decided to tell him about the Richard thing.

105
00:06:42,860 --> 00:06:44,190
What "Richard thing"?

106
00:06:44,400 --> 00:06:46,270
Oh, no.

107
00:06:48,070 --> 00:06:49,110
What "Richard thing"?

108
00:06:49,320 --> 00:06:51,110
Simmons. Go with Simmons.

109
00:06:58,290 --> 00:07:00,250
I ran into Richard yesterday.

110
00:07:00,460 --> 00:07:04,170
He asked me if I wanted to go for a bite and I did.

111
00:07:04,380 --> 00:07:06,960
I didn't tell you because you'd get mad...

112
00:07:07,170 --> 00:07:09,670
...and I didn't wanna spoil our anniversary.

113
00:07:10,260 --> 00:07:11,760
I'm not mad.

114
00:07:13,760 --> 00:07:14,800
Really?

115
00:07:16,180 --> 00:07:19,270
So you bumped into Richard. You grabbed a "bite."

116
00:07:21,850 --> 00:07:23,440
No big deal.

117
00:07:26,610 --> 00:07:27,940
Great.

118
00:07:31,570 --> 00:07:34,070
Okay, London, 1.

119
00:07:40,750 --> 00:07:42,250
Ooh.

120
00:07:54,510 --> 00:07:56,010
Hmm.

121
00:08:02,940 --> 00:08:04,560
Oh, look what happened.

122
00:08:06,940 --> 00:08:08,820
Huh, check me out.

123
00:08:09,030 --> 00:08:11,360
I'm in my kitchen...

124
00:08:11,610 --> 00:08:13,110
...naked.

125
00:08:13,950 --> 00:08:16,450
I'm picking up an orange.

126
00:08:16,950 --> 00:08:17,990
I'm naked.

127
00:08:20,790 --> 00:08:23,330
I'm lighting the candles.

128
00:08:23,540 --> 00:08:26,330
Naked. And carefully.

129
00:08:37,300 --> 00:08:40,220
Oh, my God! That's Rachel, naked!

130
00:08:42,390 --> 00:08:45,020
I can't look at that. I am looking at this.

131
00:08:45,230 --> 00:08:49,190
Okay, vivid colors, expressive brush strokes.

132
00:08:50,320 --> 00:08:54,190
Unless she wants me to be looking at that.

133
00:08:54,900 --> 00:08:56,610
She knows I'm home.

134
00:08:56,860 --> 00:08:59,740
She knows I can see her.

135
00:08:59,990 --> 00:09:03,580
What kind of game is she playing?

136
00:09:03,830 --> 00:09:07,790
I think maybe someone's lonely tonight.

137
00:09:08,460 --> 00:09:10,250
Oh, Dr. Geller.

138
00:09:10,500 --> 00:09:15,170
Stop it. You're being silly. Ha, ha.

139
00:09:15,340 --> 00:09:17,130
Or am I?

140
00:09:38,490 --> 00:09:39,820
Darn it!

141
00:09:49,420 --> 00:09:50,460
Hey.

142
00:09:55,840 --> 00:09:57,090
May I come in?

143
00:09:58,130 --> 00:09:59,800
Uh, yeah, if you want to.

144
00:10:00,800 --> 00:10:02,720
Do you want me to?

145
00:10:04,520 --> 00:10:05,640
Yeah, sure?

146
00:10:05,850 --> 00:10:07,680
So do I.

147
00:10:12,360 --> 00:10:15,820
Okay, Rach, before anything happens...

148
00:10:16,070 --> 00:10:18,780
...I wanna lay down a couple of ground rules.

149
00:10:18,990 --> 00:10:21,660
This is just about tonight.

150
00:10:21,950 --> 00:10:26,080
I won't go through with this if it'll raise the question of "us."

151
00:10:28,210 --> 00:10:29,620
I just want this to be...

152
00:10:32,750 --> 00:10:34,750
...about what it is.

153
00:10:39,010 --> 00:10:40,130
And, um...

154
00:10:40,380 --> 00:10:42,180
...what is that, Ross?

155
00:10:42,390 --> 00:10:45,010
The physical act of love.

156
00:10:46,560 --> 00:10:47,970
What, are you crazy?

157
00:10:48,180 --> 00:10:53,100
So you weren't trying to entice me just now with your nakedness?

158
00:10:55,940 --> 00:10:58,400
Oh, God. You saw me?

159
00:11:02,110 --> 00:11:06,280
You weren't trying to entice me with your nakedness?

160
00:11:06,490 --> 00:11:07,540
No!

161
00:11:07,790 --> 00:11:11,920
You actually thought I wanted to have sex with you?

162
00:11:15,750 --> 00:11:17,050
No!

163
00:11:18,880 --> 00:11:21,800
No.

164
00:11:24,350 --> 00:11:26,180
No, no, no, no.

165
00:11:49,080 --> 00:11:51,710
Hey, you guys, wait! You guys.

166
00:11:51,960 --> 00:11:54,210
This place is much better than London.

167
00:11:54,460 --> 00:11:57,090
A lady dressed like Cleopatra gave me this.

168
00:11:57,340 --> 00:11:59,920
Ninety-nine cent steak and lobster dinner. Huh.

169
00:12:00,090 --> 00:12:01,460
You don't eat animals.

170
00:12:01,720 --> 00:12:03,970
For ninety-nine cents I'd eat you.

171
00:12:05,430 --> 00:12:07,600
I can totally settle down here.

172
00:12:07,810 --> 00:12:11,980
It's got everything I could ever want. Including Joey! Look!

173
00:12:13,100 --> 00:12:14,230
Look! Hey!

174
00:12:14,690 --> 00:12:15,770
Oh, my God.

175
00:12:16,190 --> 00:12:17,810
Hey, Joey!

176
00:12:21,360 --> 00:12:22,610
- Wow!     - Hi.

177
00:12:22,820 --> 00:12:24,360
Love your condoms, my man.

178
00:12:25,780 --> 00:12:28,160
Why are you here? I told you not to come.

179
00:12:28,370 --> 00:12:30,370
Why are you dressed as a gladiator?

180
00:12:30,540 --> 00:12:35,210
Uh, because I'm shooting a scene right now. I play a gladiator.

181
00:12:36,920 --> 00:12:39,340
Hold on a second. Can we cut?

182
00:12:39,590 --> 00:12:42,090
My friends are here. I'm gonna take a break.

183
00:12:42,510 --> 00:12:44,220
Who are you talking to?

184
00:12:45,510 --> 00:12:46,590
The director.

185
00:12:46,760 --> 00:12:48,470
Uh, her.

186
00:12:51,680 --> 00:12:54,730
All right, it's not a gladiator movie. I work here.

187
00:12:54,980 --> 00:12:56,390
Why? What happened?

188
00:12:56,600 --> 00:12:58,730
The movie shut down. Ran out of money.

189
00:12:58,940 --> 00:13:02,230
I'm working here till it starts up, if it ever does.

190
00:13:02,440 --> 00:13:04,150
- I'm so sorry.     - Such a drag.

191
00:13:04,400 --> 00:13:06,610
Sorry I didn't tell you. I'm sorry.

192
00:13:06,820 --> 00:13:09,990
Apparently there's a new policy of not sharing.

193
00:13:10,200 --> 00:13:13,700
- I knew you weren't okay with that.     - So you're a gladiator!

194
00:13:14,620 --> 00:13:16,080
What's going on?

195
00:13:16,290 --> 00:13:19,170
- Monica had lunch with Richard.     - Dawson?

196
00:13:20,540 --> 00:13:21,590
No...

197
00:13:21,800 --> 00:13:24,260
But that would've been so cool!

198
00:13:24,720 --> 00:13:26,090
Her boyfriend Richard.

199
00:13:26,300 --> 00:13:30,600
It meant nothing. After all this time, how can you not trust me?

200
00:13:30,810 --> 00:13:34,270
When you go lunching with hunky men and don't tell me!

201
00:13:36,440 --> 00:13:39,270
You're right. I'm sorry. I should've told you.

202
00:13:39,860 --> 00:13:40,900
Thanks.

203
00:13:41,820 --> 00:13:44,610
- Aw, there we go.     - Now I love Vegas.

204
00:13:45,690 --> 00:13:48,780
I promise you next time I absolutely will tell you.

205
00:13:52,200 --> 00:13:53,240
"Next time"?

206
00:13:53,700 --> 00:13:55,200
Ooh, so close.

207
00:13:56,120 --> 00:13:59,250
There won't be a next time. You cannot see him again.

208
00:13:59,460 --> 00:14:03,090
I cannot see him? You can't tell me what to do.

209
00:14:03,300 --> 00:14:05,300
That's funny, I think I just did.

210
00:14:06,340 --> 00:14:09,050
If you act like this, I won't be around you.

211
00:14:09,260 --> 00:14:10,930
- Fine.     - Happy anniversary!

212
00:14:11,140 --> 00:14:13,560
Guys, please! Come on, come on.

213
00:14:13,760 --> 00:14:15,890
This is obviously a misunderstanding.

214
00:14:16,140 --> 00:14:18,100
- No, it's not.     - What're you talking about?

215
00:14:18,310 --> 00:14:20,100
Don't look at me. I just work here.

216
00:14:24,320 --> 00:14:28,990
Okay, um, Ross? I'm a little warm, so I'm gonna be taking off my sweater.

217
00:14:29,200 --> 00:14:31,780
Now, I'm just letting you know...

218
00:14:32,030 --> 00:14:36,120
...this is not an invitation to the physical act of love.

219
00:14:37,910 --> 00:14:40,080
Yep, that's hilarious.

220
00:14:40,920 --> 00:14:42,920
I'm sorry. I'm done. I'm done.

221
00:14:43,130 --> 00:14:46,250
You know, last night was embarrassing for you too.

222
00:14:46,460 --> 00:14:48,380
No, not really.

223
00:14:48,590 --> 00:14:51,380
But you know, I just don't embarrass that easily.

224
00:14:51,590 --> 00:14:53,720
What? You totally get embarrassed.

225
00:14:53,930 --> 00:14:58,520
No, I don't. Ross, I think I'm just a more secure person than you are.

226
00:14:58,730 --> 00:15:00,390
- Is that so?     - Yeah.

227
00:15:02,230 --> 00:15:03,440
Hey, lady!

228
00:15:03,650 --> 00:15:06,020
I don't care how much you want it, okay?

229
00:15:06,280 --> 00:15:09,240
I am not gonna have sex with you in the bathroom!

230
00:15:14,530 --> 00:15:17,830
You know, in Roman times, this was more than just a hat.

231
00:15:18,620 --> 00:15:19,660
Really?

232
00:15:19,870 --> 00:15:21,160
Yeah, sure, sure.

233
00:15:21,420 --> 00:15:23,420
They would scrub the floors.

234
00:15:23,670 --> 00:15:26,210
They'd use it to get the mud off their shoe.

235
00:15:26,420 --> 00:15:29,260
Sometimes underneath the horse would get dirty.

236
00:15:29,470 --> 00:15:31,260
So they would stick it right...

237
00:15:32,130 --> 00:15:35,180
I can't believe this is how I'm spending my anniversary.

238
00:15:35,390 --> 00:15:38,770
I'll take you someplace nice. A guy tipped me $100.

239
00:15:38,970 --> 00:15:40,020
- Whoa!      - Yeah.

240
00:15:40,230 --> 00:15:43,480
He was playing blackjack for an hour and he won $5000.

241
00:15:43,730 --> 00:15:45,400
Can you believe that?

242
00:15:45,610 --> 00:15:47,820
If I won $5000, I'd join a gym.

243
00:15:48,030 --> 00:15:49,480
Build up my upper body...

244
00:15:49,690 --> 00:15:52,200
...and hit Richard from behind with a stick.

245
00:15:53,530 --> 00:15:56,280
Wait! Why don't I just do what that guy did?

246
00:15:56,530 --> 00:15:58,700
I'll take this $100, turn it into $5000...

247
00:15:58,950 --> 00:16:02,210
...and I'll turn that into enough to get my movie going!

248
00:16:03,210 --> 00:16:04,500
Good luck.

249
00:16:04,710 --> 00:16:08,210
- I don't need luck. I've thought this through.     - I see.

250
00:16:13,340 --> 00:16:15,090
- Thank you.     - Thanks.

251
00:16:15,680 --> 00:16:19,100
I can't believe this. This is like the worst night ever.

252
00:16:19,310 --> 00:16:22,730
You had a minor setback in your relationship.

253
00:16:22,980 --> 00:16:24,640
Big deal. It's only Chandler.

254
00:16:26,520 --> 00:16:29,190
I am so sorry.

255
00:16:31,070 --> 00:16:34,200
This is crazy having such a stupid argument.

256
00:16:34,450 --> 00:16:36,160
I don't wanna see Richard.

257
00:16:36,370 --> 00:16:38,320
So go fix it.

258
00:16:38,580 --> 00:16:41,240
Find Chandler. He's probably in your room.

259
00:16:41,500 --> 00:16:43,370
Tell him sorry and you love him.

260
00:16:43,910 --> 00:16:45,670
You're right, Phoebe.

261
00:16:45,870 --> 00:16:47,330
- Thank you.     - Sure.

